{"name":"Incubus","hex":"#772222","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"incubus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evil spirit supposed to oppress people while asleep, especially to have sex with women as they sleep.","A feeling of oppression during sleep, sleep paralysis; night terrors, a nightmare."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incubus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Incubus","blocks":[{"text":"An incubus is a male demon who is described in various folklore as appearing in the dreams of female humans in order to seduce them. Repeated interactions between an incubus and a woman will lead to sexual activity, a bond forming between them, and ultimately sexual intercourse, as he requires vaginal ejaculation discharge to survive. The establishment and perpetuation of such a relationship enables the production of a hybrid child known as a cambion, but at the expense of the woman, whose mental and physical health will deteriorate rapidly, eventually resulting in her death if the incubus continues courting her for a protracted period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Incubus.jpg/330px-Incubus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incubus","wikidata":"Q378070"},{"title":"Incubus (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Incubus is an American rock band from Calabasas, California. The band was formed in 1991 by vocalist Brandon Boyd, lead guitarist Mike Einziger, and drummer José Pasillas while enrolled in Calabasas High School and later expanded to include bassist Alex \"Dirk Lance\" Katunich, and Gavin \"DJ Lyfe\" Koppel; the latter two were eventually replaced by bassist Ben Kenney and DJ Kilmore, respectively. Nicole Row replaced Kenney in 2024."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Incubus_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_2023-08-05_09.jpg/330px-Incubus_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_2023-08-05_09.jp